{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0141","billNumberShort":"H.B. 141","billNumberLong":"HB0141S01","fileNumber":"2026FL0032","shortTitle":"International Money Transmission Amendments","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"GRICIS","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Gricius, Stephanie","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"MCCAYD","floorSponsorName":"Sen. McCay, Daniel","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill enacts provisions related to international money transmissions.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>imposes a tax on international money transmissions on or after a certain date;<hr><ltbullet>exempts an international money transmission from the tax if the customer requesting the transaction presents valid identification;<hr><ltbullet>requires the tax to be stated separately on an invoice or receipt;<hr><ltbullet>requires licensed money transmitters to remit collected taxes quarterly and report annually to the State Tax Commission;<hr><ltbullet>provides for the State Tax Commission's administration of the tax;<hr><ltbullet>requires the commissioner of the Department of Financial Institutions to annually provide a list of each licensed money transmitter to the State Tax Commission; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Gus Harb","fiscalAnalyst":"Andrea Wilko","lastAction":"House/ filed","lastActionOwner":"House file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/2026","trackingID":"RNDDHVNJIG","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-05 12:31:28.597","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-05 12:31:28.597